,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/pulls/10852","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/10852","diff_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/10852.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/10852.patch","merged_at":"2021-11-10T16:24:47Z"},"body":"# Makes `Enum` members implicitly `final`\r\n\r\nMy problem was that this code was typechecking:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom enum import Enum\r\n\r\nclass A(str, Enum):\r\n    some = 'some'\r\n    other = 'other'\r\n\r\nA.some = 'new'\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhile in runtime it was failing with:\r\n\r\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"ex.py\", line 12, in <module>\r\n    A.some = 'new'\r\n  File \"/Users/sobolev/.pyenv/versions/3.8.9/lib/python3.8/enum.py\", line 427, in __setattr__\r\n    raise AttributeError('Cannot reassign members.')\r\nAttributeError: Cannot reassign members.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis change allows to catch this error by making all `Enum` members implicitly `Final`.\r\n\r\nI also had to modify `Enum` plugin, since it was not ready to work with `Literal[True]` and `Literal[False]`.\r\n\r\nCloses #5599 \r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\nI would love to hear your feedback! 👍 ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/10852/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/10852/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"sobolevn","id":4660275,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjAyNzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4660275?v=4","gravatar_id":"",